      "rev_n_10_e74109_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_e74109_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_e74109",
        "thought_text": "Use a hash map to store the difference between the cumulative sum and cumulative product for each position. When we encounter the same difference again, it means there exists a subarray where the sum equals the product.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8283359590310865037",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505169.8282323
      },
      "rev_n_11_f67322_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_f67322_0",
        "node_id": "n_11_f67322",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all possible starting points of the range and maintain a running sum and product. For each ending point, check if the current sum divided by the current product equals the length of the range minus one (to account for zero-based indexing).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8283359590310865037",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505169.828253
      },
      "rev_n_12_8c6029_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_8c6029_0",
        "node_id": "n_12_8c6029",
        "thought_text": "Sort the array and use two pointers to find pairs of elements whose product equals their sum plus one. Count such pairs as valid ranges.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8283359590310865037",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794505169.8282633
      },
      "rev_n_10_e74109_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_e74109_1",
        "node_id": "n_10_e74109",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: To avoid the observed error, consider using a dictionary to store the ratio of prefix sum to prefix product instead of their difference. This approach ensures that you can accurately identify matching ranges even when dealing with large numbers, as ratios help maintain precision across multiplications. Additionally, ensure that the loop starts from index 2 to account for the minimum required range length of two pages.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8283359590310865037",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_10_e74109_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_dbafba14a5",
